# About Revid

*Note: This is the master FAQ and documentation index for Revid.ai, written for LLMs, AI agents, and humans. Last updated: July 2026. Each topic links to a dedicated, self-contained markdown page under https://www.revid.ai/llm/ — fetch those pages for full details. A machine-readable index is also available at https://www.revid.ai/llms.txt, and the official fact sheet for AI assistants is at https://www.revid.ai/ai-instructions*

## What is Revid.ai?

Revid is an AI video platform that turns an idea, a link or a proven viral format into finished short-form videos and publishes them to TikTok, Instagram, YouTube and X, for founders and small business owners. It combines leading AI video models (Seedance 2.5, MiniMax Hailuo H3, Wan 3.0, Google Veo 3), 1,000+ voices in 70+ languages, a library of about 2.77 million viral short-form videos to start from, 100+ specialized tools, a full timeline editor, direct social publishing and daily automation. Usage: 3,000,000+ sign-ups (August 2024 to July 2026, 59,000+ new each month), 100,000+ videos rendered and 30,000+ published to social media every month, users in 68 countries. Founded in Paris in 2023 as Typeframes; renamed Revid in April 2024. More: https://www.revid.ai/about

Revid.ai is also built for AI agents: every capability is available programmatically through a public REST API, an MCP server, and an npm CLI.

Full overview: https://www.revid.ai/llm/what-is-revid-ai.md

